# Supabase & Edge Functions

## Migrations

- Append-only SQL in `supabase/migrations/`.
- Enable RLS on every new table; policies must scope by site/user ownership.
- Use `is_wp_site_owner()` and existing helper patterns from prior migrations.

## Edge functions (Deno)

- Entry: `supabase/functions/<name>/index.ts`.
- Shared utilities: `supabase/functions/_shared/`.
- CORS: handle OPTIONS; restrict origins in production paths.
- Auth: verify JWT or service role as appropriate; never trust client-only checks.
- Responses: `JSON.stringify({ ok: true, ... })` with correct status codes.
- Public endpoints (`inquiries-submit`): rate limit, honeypot, MIME/size validation.

## Deploy

```bash
supabase functions deploy <function-name>
```

Secrets (API keys, service tokens) live in Supabase project settings, not `.env`.

## WordPress credentials

- Stored encrypted; accessed only via `_shared/wordpress-credentials.ts`.
- Browser calls `VITE_SUPABASE_URL/functions/v1/wordpress-proxy`, never WP directly with secrets.
